this monitoring service making it faster to begin monitoring the health and performance of your virtual machines.
 
VM insights provides a quick and easy method for getting started monitoring the client workloads on your virtual machines and virtual machine scale sets.
It displays an inventory of your existing VMs and provides a guided experience to enable base monitoring for them. 
It also monitors the performance of your virtual machines and virtual machine scale sets by collecting data on their running processes and dependencies on other resources.
 
VMinsight, basically use to monitor VM guest Data and its supports Windows and Linux operating both.

Note: Once you enable VM Insights, it will create a Data Collection Rule (DCR) and install the Azure Monitor Agent on the VM.
This agent collects common performance counters for the client operating system and sends them to the Insights Metrics table in the Log Analytics workspace.

> Now your question should be, what is Log Analytics workspace?

So, Log Analytics workspace is a data store service, we can collect any type of log data from all of your Azure and non-Azure resources and applications. 
Workspace configuration options let you manage all of your log data in one workspace to meet the operations, analysis, and auditing needs of different personas
in your organization through:
1) Azure Monitor features, such as built-in insights experiences, alerts, and automatic actions
2) Other Azure services, such as Microsoft Sentinel, Microsoft Defender for Cloud, and Logic Apps
3) Microsoft tools, such as Power BI and Excel
4) Integration with custom and third-party applications
 
# Now lets understand, DCR(data collection rule):

Data collection rules (DCRs) define data collection from the Azure Monitor Agent and are stored in your Azure subscription. 
For VMs, DCRs define data such as events and performance counters to collect, and specify locations such as Log Analytics workspaces to send the data.
A single VM can be associated with multiple DCRs, and a single DCR can be associated with multiple VMs.

#And what is Azure Monitor Agent?
The Azure Monitor Agent is responsible to collects monitoring data from the guest operating system of Azure and hybrid virtual machines (VMs). 
It delivers the data to Azure Monitor for use by features, insights, and other services, such as Microsoft Sentinel and Microsoft Defender for Cloud.

