> Processes refer to the list of the running active (like nginx, sqlserver etc.) on a VM.

Its Show CPU, memory, and network usage by each process.
Helps to identify unusual processes.
Useful for troubleshooting performance issues on the VM.

> And Dependencies refer to the network connections and interactions of the VM with other machines, services, or processes— whether on-premises, in Azure, or external.

Its Shows inbound/outbound connections from the VM.

Visualizes dependency maps between services and servers.

Helps to identify bottlenecks, latency, and unusual connections

> What is a Dependency Map?

The Dependency Map is a visual tool in Azure Monitor for VMs that displays how your VM is connected to other systems.

What It Shows:

Your VM and all the processes running on it.

The outbound and inbound connections of each process.

Remote machines or endpoints the VM talks to.

Connection metrics like:

Latency

Connection count

Failure rate

Note: Once we enabled Processes and Dependencies, it will install Dependency agent on the VM. and  Network connectivity will be allowed for monitoring traffic.

> Dependency agent:
Dependency Agent collects data about processes running on the virtual machine and their external process dependencies.
